CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ f: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ h: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
convert_function_template gave both templates the same identifier (the
method qualifier is not part of the function type), so the const one became
a SFINAE alternative of the non-const one and `cw.f(0)' found no match.
Found in libc++'s std::views::take closure (__perfect_forward_impl's
operator() overloads).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
